  "verbalization": "Heparin is implicated in the interaction with U251 through multiple pathways, with SNU-387 acting as a common target in all three connections. The first pathway links heparin to SNU-387, which is then targeted by a compound called Dendocarbin K, and finally, SNU-387 is shown to target U251. This suggests a potential mechanism where heparin may influence SNU-387, which in turn affects U251. The evidence is consistent across different targets of SNU-387, indicating a possible role in a broader biological process. The integration of these pathways highlights the involvement of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the relationship between heparin and U251, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
